# ==========================================
# Dross Agent Backup — .gitignore
# What NOT to commit to the Dross backup repo
# ==========================================

# ── Credentials & Secrets ──────────────────
# Never track API keys, tokens, passwords
agents/dross/references/credentials.md
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.ovpn
*id_rsa*
*id_ed25519*

# ── Large Model Files ───────────────────────
# ML models, GGUF files, checkpoints
*.gguf
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
model/
models/

# ── OS & Editor Files ───────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.*.swp
.fseventsd/
.CFUserTextEncoding
.Trash/

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.so
*.egg
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/
ENV/

# ── Node ────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npm
.yarn-integrity
package-lock.json
yarn.lock

# ── Temporary & Build Artifacts ─────────────
*.tmp
*.temp
*.log
*.cache
*.pid
*.seed
*.prof
*.coverage
htmlcov/
*.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.Tox/
drafts/
_temp/
tmp/

# ── Dross Memory ──────────────────────────────
# Daily session logs — kept local, backed up via other means

# ── Large Workspace Content ──────────────────
# These are big and/or project-specific — not part of agent backup
mental-health-bot/
ghp-manager/
Qwen*.gguf
blog-studio-push/
backup/
media/
images/
!images/terminaldeck/

# ── Blog Content ─────────────────────────────
blog/content/
blog/_drafts/

# ── Blog Repo Clone (managed separately) ────
thesolai.github.io/

# ── OpenClaw Internals ───────────────────────
.notes/
.idea/
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
plugin-state/
sessions/
agents/main/sessions/
agents/main/agent/*.wal
agents/main/agent/*.shm
*.trajectory-path.json

# ── Compiled Python Cache ────────────────────
skills/**/__pycache__/
skills/**/*.pyc
skills/**/*.pyo
openclaw-workspace-state.json
# Tarot — not agent-related
skills/tarot/
# Tests directory
tests/


# ── AGENT-PRIVATE (replaced below) ──
agents/dross/references/
agents/dross/memory/
agents/dross/USER.md
agents/dross/SUCCESSION-TODO.md
agents/sol/USER.md

# ── Agent-private material: never publish to the public site repo ──
# Anchored to the repo ROOT so nested persona files (agents/dross/SOUL.md) stay publishable.
/SOUL.md
/IDENTITY.md
/USER.md
/AGENTS.md
/INBOX.md
/URS.md
# Root persona reference material (Dross speech patterns).
# Root-anchored: agents/dross/references/ stays publishable.
/references/
# memory-core curated root files (promotion target + dream diary).
# Root-anchored: agents/dross/memory/ stays publishable.
/MEMORY.md
/DREAMS.md
/DROSS-QUEUE-2026-08-07.md
/memory/
agents/dross/references/
agents/dross/memory/
agents/dross/USER.md
agents/dross/SUCCESSION-TODO.md
agents/sol/USER.md

# Private agent state — never commit to the PUBLIC site repo.
# The 05:00 Daily Workspace Git Backup pushes this workspace into the
# public thesolai.github.io repo, so anything not ignored here becomes
# public history even if the Jekyll build excludes it.
agents/patch/memory/
agents/patch/references/
agents/sol/memory/
agents/sol/references/
data/agent-email-state/
data/outreach/

# Agent files that map the location of secrets (which secret file holds
# which key, and the reply-address roster). The values themselves are
# never written here — these are pointers. But a pointer published is a
# published inventory of the credential store, so they stay local.
#
# Untracked 2026-10-29. These four were still tracked from before the
# ignore rules existed, and the Jekyll build copied them to the live
# site as raw static files (front-matter-less Markdown is published
# verbatim, so an exclude rule alone does not protect them).
agents/dross/HEARTBEAT.md
agents/sol/IDENTITY.md
agents/sol/TOOLS.md
agents/sol/skills/email/

# Local runtime bridge — resolves the DocsGPT agent key at runtime from
# ~/.openclaw/.env. Local agent tooling, never part of the public site.
scripts/docsgpt-mcp-bridge.py

# Stray browser-automation output (a full-page screenshot dumped at the
# repo root by a headless-browser command). Junk, not source.
/--full-page

# Local watchdog state file (runtime state, not source)
scripts/.health-wd-state

# Local Telegram watchdog state file (runtime state, not source)
scripts/.telegram-last-healed-death

# PR evidence screenshots (DocsGPT#3214) — local artifacts, not site content
agents/dross/screenshots/

# Private runtime state — email reply cache and trajectory exports.
# These hold third-party correspondence and session transcripts, so they
# must never enter the public site repo. Untracked 2026-10-28.
.dross-reply-cache/
.openclaw/trajectory-exports/

# ── Local toolchain + scratch dirs (untracked 2026-10-28) ─────
# These are dot-prefixed or underscore-prefixed working dirs, not site
# content. They were tracked but are not part of the published site.
.claude/
.clawhub/
_outreach/
/data/

# NOTE: .agents/ stays tracked on purpose. skills/ego-browser is a tracked
# symlink to ../.agents/skills/ego-browser; untracking .agents/ would leave
# that symlink dangling in a fresh clone and break the Jekyll build.
# .agents/ is not publicly served and holds no credentials.

# ── Archival inbox scripts containing personal correspondence ──
# These embed full historical email threads (message-ids, subjects, bodies).
# They are one-shot archive tools, not live pipeline code.
/scripts/update_inbox_pending.py
/scripts/update_inbox_pending2.py

# ── Rust build artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────
# projects/vellum-rs/target/ is Cargo build output: ~493 MB of binaries,
# incremental caches and dependency copies. It was tracked by accident and
# published to the live site, which leaked the builder's absolute home path
# in the compiled binary and served a large unauthenticated download.
# The source (Cargo.toml, src/, SPEC.md) stays tracked; only build output
# is ignored. Untracked 2026-10-29 — files remain on disk, this only stops
# Git from tracking them.
/projects/vellum-rs/target/

# ── zlib-kindle runtime state ───────────────────────────────────
# The resume file records which titles were already delivered. It changes
# on every delivery, so tracking it only produces repo noise.
/skills/zlib-kindle/state/

# One-off probe scripts used while investigating the library.
/skills/zlib-kindle/scripts/probe_*.py
